1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,224
Friday, November 27 is Black Friday.

2
00:00:03,274 --> 00:00:08,702
French shoppers plan to spend
151 euros on average.

3
00:00:08,752 --> 00:00:12,556
But last year, when Europe
checked online deals,

4
00:00:12,606 --> 00:00:15,447
almost one in three broke the rules.

5
00:00:15,497 --> 00:00:18,332
So how do you know if a deal is real?

6
00:00:18,382 --> 00:00:23,124
We investigated. And the answer takes
thirty seconds, with AI.

7
00:00:23,370 --> 00:00:27,023
Black Friday and Cyber Monday 2025.

8
00:00:27,073 --> 00:00:30,646
The European Commission and, in France,

9
00:00:30,696 --> 00:00:36,314
the DGCCRF screen 314 online sellers
and thousands of offers.

10
00:00:36,364 --> 00:00:41,861
The result: about thirty percent of the deals
break the price display rules.

11
00:00:41,911 --> 00:00:48,910
And almost one seller in five uses traps: fake
countdowns, fake low-stock warnings.

12
00:00:49,160 --> 00:00:51,385
The tricks are well known.

13
00:00:51,435 --> 00:00:53,959
An inflated reference price.

14
00:00:54,009 --> 00:00:58,388
A price that goes up right before the
sale, to come down again.

15
00:00:58,438 --> 00:01:02,295
Or a comparison price, without
saying where it comes from.

16
00:01:02,550 --> 00:01:04,818
Yet the rule is simple.

17
00:01:04,868 --> 00:01:10,393
A discount is calculated on the lowest
price of the last thirty days.

18
00:01:10,443 --> 00:01:16,350
Another comparison price is allowed, but
its source must be stated.

19
00:01:16,600 --> 00:01:20,221
We checked a real offer, on November 21.

20
00:01:20,271 --> 00:01:23,413
A controller shown at 29 percent off.

21
00:01:23,463 --> 00:01:25,957
But look at the line below.

22
00:01:26,007 --> 00:01:31,152
Calculated on the last thirty days, the
discount is only 14 percent.

23
00:01:31,202 --> 00:01:34,929
The 29 percent is based on the
recommended price.

24
00:01:35,180 --> 00:01:40,195
To go further, you need the price
history and the other sellers.

25
00:01:40,245 --> 00:01:42,470
By hand, that takes time.

26
00:01:42,520 --> 00:01:46,256
With an AI that searches the
web, thirty seconds.

27
00:01:46,306 --> 00:01:51,688
And almost one Black Friday shopper in two
has already used AI for shopping.

28
00:01:51,940 --> 00:01:54,212
Copy the product link.

29
00:01:54,262 --> 00:01:57,704
Open Claude, ChatGPT or Gemini.

30
00:01:57,754 --> 00:02:02,609
Paste the link, and ask: is
this a real deal?

31
00:02:02,659 --> 00:02:08,758
Look up the price history and the price
elsewhere, answer in three lines,

32
00:02:08,808 --> 00:02:10,274
with your sources.

33
00:02:10,520 --> 00:02:15,972
Here, the AI answers: a real deal,
but not the best one.

34
00:02:16,022 --> 00:02:21,668
On Black Friday 2024, this controller
was already 54.99 euros.

35
00:02:21,718 --> 00:02:25,814
And another site sells it
one euro cheaper.

36
00:02:25,864 --> 00:02:28,708
Its advice: wait.

37
00:02:28,960 --> 00:02:31,756
Careful: the AI can be wrong.

38
00:02:31,806 --> 00:02:35,582
Here, it says itself that it
couldn't open the page.

39
00:02:35,632 --> 00:02:39,959
Click its sources, and compare
exactly the same model.

40
00:02:40,210 --> 00:02:42,988
Black Friday lasts a few days.

41
00:02:43,038 --> 00:02:45,556
Fake deals, all year long.

42
00:02:45,606 --> 00:02:49,349
Thirty seconds of checking is enough.

43
00:02:49,399 --> 00:02:53,073
The exact question is in the description.

44
00:02:53,123 --> 00:02:56,478
Subscribe for more
investigations and AI tips.

